ate names on the stack, bottom-first.\nClassify the first line of an input stream by its leading bytes\nand drop a UTF-8 byte-order mark. run and run_file do this\nthemselves; it is public for a caller that reads its own lines\nand hands them to dispatch .  An unallocated text is ENC_PLAIN .\nDisplay name of an ENC_* value, as used in the engine's messages. .true. for the encodings the engine reads: ENC_PLAIN and ENC_UTF8_BOM . public pure elemental module function encoding_supported(enc) result(ok) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: enc Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface/encoding_supported.html"},{"title":"strip_bom – cmdgraph","text":"interface Add a concrete state (has a prompt) or abstract state (mix-in, no prompt).\nAdd a command edge to state .\nBuild an integer arg_spec_t .\nBuild a real arg_spec_t .\nBuild a character arg_spec_t .\nBuild a rest arg_spec_t (verbatim remainder of the line; must be last).\nReturn n copies of an integer spec (fixed-size tuple, e.g. a 2D point).\nReturn n copies of a real spec.\nSuccessful result, optionally carrying a DoGoto context string.\nError result, optionally with a message written to the error channel.\nMerge all commands from abstract state included into state .\nThe state's own commands override included ones with the same spec.\nRegister a hook called after every successful transition into state .\nValidate the graph and set the initial state.\nSets stat non-zero if a cycle is detected in goto/do_goto edges\nor if any state reference is unresolved.\nRun an interactive loop reading from the configured input stream.\nThe loop ends at end of input, on quit, or - having written the\nreason to the error channel - at a line in an unsupported encoding.\nExecute commands from path , stopping at the first error.\nReturns .true. if the file ran to completion (or ended with quit).\nRewind to the initial state without rebuilding the graph.\nClears the stack, contexts, last_message , and last_error .\nRedirect I/O channels.  Pass QUIET_UNIT to suppress a channel.\nDefault: stdin / stdout / stderr .\nDispatch one line of input.\nPerforms prefix matching, arg validation, and edge traversal.\nName of the active state.\nContext of the active state.\nReturns .false. after Quit or stack exhausted.\nCommands visible in the current state (own + included, help/? excluded).\nResult depends only on the state name; safe to cache keyed by state name.\nState names on the stack, bottom-first.\nClassify the first line of an input stream by its leading bytes\nand drop a UTF-8 byte-order mark. run and run_file do this\nthemselves; it is public for a caller that reads its own lines\nand hands them to dispatch .  An unallocated text is ENC_PLAIN .\nDisplay name of an ENC_* value, as used in the engine's messages. .true. for the encodings the engine reads: ENC_PLAIN and ENC_UTF8_BOM . public pure module subroutine strip_bom(text, enc) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=:), intent(inout), allocatable :: text First line; a UTF-8 mark is removed integer, intent(out) :: enc One of the ENC_* values","tags":"","url":"interface/strip_bom.html"},{"title":"int_node – cmdgraph","text":"public interface int_node Module Procedures public  interface make_int_node () Arguments None","tags":"","url":"interface/int_node.html"},{"title":"real_node – cmdgraph","text":"public interface real_node Module Procedures public  interface make_real_node () Arguments None","tags":"","url":"interface/real_node.html"},{"title":"real_a_node – cmdgraph","text":"public interface real_a_node Module Procedures public  interface make_real_a_node () Arguments None","tags":"","url":"interface/real_a_node.html"},{"title":"real_m_node – cmdgraph","text":"public interface real_m_node Module Procedures public  interface make_real_m_node () Arguments None","tags":"","url":"interface/real_m_node.html"},{"title":"char_node – cmdgraph","text":"public interface char_node Module Procedures public  interface make_char_node () Arguments None","tags":"","url":"interface/char_node.html"},{"title":"make_node – cmdgraph","text":"public interface make_node Module Procedures public  interface make_int_node () Arguments None public  interface make_real_node () Arguments None public  interface make_real_a_node () Arguments None public  interface make_real_m_node () Arguments None public  interface make_char_node () Arguments None","tags":"","url":"interface/make_node.html"},{"title":"make_int_node – cmdgraph","text":"interface public module function make_int_node(v) result(n) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: v Return Value type( dlist_node_integer )","tags":"","url":"interface/make_int_node.html"},{"title":"make_real_node – cmdgraph","text":"interface public module function make_real_node(v) result(n) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: v Return Value type( dlist_node_real )","tags":"","url":"interface/make_real_node.html"},{"title":"make_real_a_node – cmdgraph","text":"interface public module function make_real_a_node(v) result(n) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: v (:) Return Value type( dlist_node_real_a )","tags":"","url":"interface/make_real_a_node.html"},{"title":"make_real_m_node – cmdgraph","text":"interface public module function make_real_m_node(v) result(n) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: v (:,:) Return Value type( dlist_node_real_m )","tags":"","url":"interface/make_real_m_node.html"},{"title":"make_char_node – cmdgraph","text":"interface public module function make_char_node(v) result(n) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: v Return Value type( dlist_node_char )","tags":"","url":"interface/make_char_node.html"},{"title":"iterate_ll – cmdgraph","text":"interface Apply f to each element in forward order.\nReturns .true. if all elements were visited (i.e. f never set ok=.false. ).\nInsert data at 1-based idx , shifting later elements right.\nOut-of-range low values prepend; out-of-range high values append.\nRemove the element at 1-based idx .\nSilently does nothing if idx is out-of-range.\nReplace the data at 1-based idx in place (one walk, no node churn).\nThe new data may be a different dynamic type than the old.\nSilently does nothing if idx is out-of-range (matching remove ).\nApply f to each element in reverse order.\nPrint list contents to unit (default output_unit ).\nRenders the built-in node kinds; extensions print as <user-defined> .\nAppend data to the tail of the list.\nNumber of elements in the list.\nRemove all elements.\nIndex-based accessor (1-based).  Returns an allocatable polymorphic\ncopy of the node data.  Unallocated if idx is out of range —\ncheck allocated(node) before select type . public module function iterate_ll(this, f) result(r) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( dlist_t ), intent(inout), target :: this procedure( command_fun ) :: f Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface/iterate_ll.html"},{"title":"reverse_iterate_ll – cmdgraph","text":"interface Apply f to each element in forward order.\nReturns .true. if all elements were visited (i.e. f never set ok=.false. ).\nInsert data at 1-based idx , shifting later elements right.\nOut-of-range low values prepend; out-of-range high values append.\nRemove the element at 1-based idx .\nSilently does nothing if idx is out-of-range.\nReplace the data at 1-based idx in place (one walk, no node churn).\nThe new data may be a different dynamic type than the old.\nSilently does nothing if idx is out-of-range (matching remove ).\nApply f to each element in reverse order.\nPrint list contents to unit (default output_unit ).\nRenders the built-in node kinds; extensions print as <user-defined> .\nAppend data to the tail of the list.\nNumber of elements in the list.\nRemove all elements.\nIndex-based accessor (1-based)